        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಮೊದಲನೆಯ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮೊದಲನೆಯ (modalaneya) — \"first\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ending is the one you already have. What is new is the word underneath it, because there is no ಒಂದು anywhere in modalaneya — and there was never going to be."
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "cardinal",
                "ordinal"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 3,
              "utterances": [
                "cardinal: ಒಂದು (ondu). ordinal: ಮೊದಲನೆಯ (modalaneya).",
                "cardinal: ಎರಡು (eraḍu). ordinal: ಎರಡನೆಯ (eraḍaneya).",
                "cardinal: ಮೂರು (mūru). ordinal: ಮೂರನೆಯ (mūraneya)."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮೊದಲನೆಯ ದಿನ (modalaneya dina), the first day. ಮೊದಲನೆಯ ದಾರಿ (modalaneya dāri), the first road."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "cognates",
          "title": "Across the family: ಮೊದಲು, \"a beginning\"",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Under it sits ಮೊದಲು (modalu), \"a beginning\" — so the word means \"of the beginning\", not \"one-th\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "language",
                "\"one\"",
                "\"first\" is built on"
              ],
              "columns": 3,
              "rowCount": 3,
              "utterances": [
                "language: Kannada. \"one\": ondu. \"first\" is built on: ಮೊದಲು modalu, a beginning.",
                "language: Tamil. \"one\": oṉṟu. \"first\" is built on: முதல் mudal, a beginning.",
                "language: Telugu. \"one\": okaṭi. \"first\" is built on: మొదలు modalu, a beginning."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three sisters, three different words for one, and the same word for the start of a line. Counting and ordering were never the same idea in this family, and first is where the seam shows."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Note what is and is not irregular here. The ending is perfectly regular — modalu drops its final -ು and takes -ಅನೆಯ exactly like eraḍu did. It is only the stem that is a surprise. Kannada asks you to learn one extra word, not one extra rule."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
