              "columns": 3,
              "rowCount": 5,
              "utterances": [
                "1. cardinal: ಒಂದು ondu. ordinal: ಮೊದಲನೆಯ modalaneya.",
                "2. cardinal: ಎರಡು eraḍu. ordinal: ಎರಡನೆಯ eraḍaneya.",
                "3. cardinal: ಮೂರು mūru. ordinal: ಮೂರನೆಯ mūraneya.",
                "4. cardinal: ನಾಲ್ಕು nālku. ordinal: ನಾಲ್ಕನೆಯ nālkaneya.",
                "5. cardinal: ಐದು aidu. ordinal: ಐದನೆಯ aidaneya."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Count the work. Four of those five were built, from numbers you had learned when you learned to count and an ending you learned in one lesson. Exactly one, modalaneya, was a word to learn — and even it took the regular ending."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English asks you to learn first, second, third before the pattern starts; Latin asks for ten separate words. Kannada asks for one, and it is not a number word at all."
            }
          ]
        },
